# C1-S04 to C1-S07 — the North Field, Field Fracture, the Boar, the Bridge Warning.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1654–1735.
# Refusing to help doesn't end the game: time passes, villagers get hurt, and
# the story carries on through the aftermath. Nobody calls Kaelen a villain.
# rhythm: clipped boar_fight_staged
# (Shouted combat calls during the staged boar fight.)

# C1-S04: the bell rings twice, then stutters.
~ alarm
do bell_alarm
Farmer: The north field! It's split right down the middle, and it's still going!
do elara_stands
Kaelen: Split how? Cracked, like an earthquake? Or the other kind?
Elara: You'll see soon enough. Lantern's by the door, and my hands are full.
? Kaelen (Internal): She's already out the door. She didn't wait to see if I'd follow.
- I'm coming with you. => help
- This isn't my... I've been here half a day. I'd only be in the way. => hesitate

~ help
set ch1_north_field_helped
do trust elara 10
Elara: Keep up, stranger. Anything out there that flickers, you go round it, not through it.

~ hesitate
Mara: Still here? Think we can't look after ourselves, love? And who do you reckon gets down the south road with that field split? Not you.
do fracture_spreads
? Kaelen (Internal): It's spreading toward the houses. Faster than a crack should, and in a straighter line.
- That's heading for the houses. I'm coming. => help
- I'm staying here. => refuse

~ refuse
set ch1_north_field_refused
do trust elara -10
Mara: Suit yourself. Kettle's going on, and I'm getting the bandages down. Someone'll need both.

# C1-S05: the irrigation water is flowing uphill. Data Vision shows why.
~ field_water
System: SYSTEM TRACE: WATER_SIM RULESET CONFLICT.
System: VERSION A17. VERSION B04.
Kaelen: That's two sets of rules running at once, and they're both trying to tell the same water where to go.
Elara: Then one of them has to stop. Can you do that, or do I fetch shovels?
Kaelen: Maybe. If I pick the right one. If I pick the wrong one, the water goes— I don't actually know where.
Elara: "Maybe" has never once dug a ditch round here. Pick the right one, then.
? Kaelen (Internal): The sluice is where the two rules meet. Which way do I fix it?
- Edit it. Let the ground as it is now win. => edit_terrain
- Edit it. Wall this channel off so nothing else touches it. => edit_isolate
- Leave the code alone. Borrow a shovel and dig a new channel. => dig

~ edit_terrain
set ch1_sluice_edited
do root_edit sluice terrain_priority
Elara: Is that fixed, or is it fixed until I turn my back?
Kaelen: For now. Downhill's winning again. I'd want to watch it through a proper rain before I promised more.
Elara: Rain's due tonight. You'll get your test whether you want it or not.

~ edit_isolate
set ch1_sluice_isolated
do root_edit sluice isolate
Elara: Wenna's going to walk out to her beans tomorrow and wonder where her water went. You can explain it to her.
Kaelen: I'll tell her. I'll leave out the part where I'm not sure where it went either.

~ dig
set ch1_sluice_dug
do dig_channel
Elara: Your trick would've had that done before I'd even found a shovel.
Kaelen: Probably. But if the trick breaks, I want something under it that doesn't. A ditch doesn't need me to keep working.
do trust elara 10
Elara: Huh. Pass me the other shovel. I'll take the far end.

# C1-S06: a corrupted boar guarding an erased nest. Data Vision shows DEFEND NEST
# with a null nest reference, the same error as the guardian on the road.
~ boar
Kaelen: Same error as the guardian on the road. It's guarding a nest that isn't there anymore.
Elara: Then it's not a monster. It's a mother with nowhere to be a mother.
? Kaelen (Internal): It's pawing the ground, still facing where the nest should be. What do I do about it?
- Fight it. => boar_fight
- Turn its aggression down. Leave the rest of it alone. => boar_calm
- Give it a nest. Something close enough to fool it. => boar_nest

~ boar_fight
set ch1_boar_fought
do start_boar_fight

~ boar_calm
set ch1_boar_calmed
do root_edit boar aggression

~ boar_nest
set ch1_boar_nest_rebuilt
do trust elara 10
Elara: Moss from the ditch, sticks off the fence, and whatever it is you do with your hands. Quickly, before she charges.
do boar_nest_anchor

# Later, at Mara's, if the nest was rebuilt.
~ mara_boar
Mara: A boar, love? You built a boar a house? Was there a door, or did you leave that bit to her?
Kaelen: A nest. Mostly moss. It needed something there so it could stop guarding nothing.
Mara: Guarding nothing? Half the men in this village do that all day outside my shop, and nobody builds them a nest.
Old Fen: Guarding nothing, she says.
Mara: You were meant to hear that, Fen. Shut the door, you're letting the heat out.

# C1-S07: the north bridge is badly fractured. The first explicit deadline.
~ bridge
Bran: North bridge is cracked right through. I got my fingers in it to the knuckle. Rain tonight, and when the river comes up, it's going in.
Kaelen: How long before the river comes up? In hours, please, if you've got them.
Bran: I don't do hours for weather. Until dark. That's at the top of today's page now, above the goats and the caravans.
do quest_start bridge_before_dark
? Kaelen (Internal): One deadline, and two places I need to be. The bridge, or Aldric's trail?
- Leave it with me. It'll be fixed before dark. => bridge_fix
- If I can't fix it, at least keep everyone off it. => bridge_warn
- I can't. It'll have to wait. => bridge_wait

~ bridge_fix
set ch1_bridge_repair_accepted
Bran: Then I'm writing it now, before you change your mind: north bridge, "fixed by the crater". Don't make a liar of my ink.

~ bridge_warn
set ch1_bridge_evacuated
Bran: A man at each end, then. Two of the Pell boys; they're big and they're idle. They'll complain, and I'll write the complaining down too.

~ bridge_wait
set ch1_bridge_ignored
Bran: I'm not writing that down. It's your road too, you know. You walked in on it with crater on your boots.

# The bridge outcome is set by the scene at dark: ch1_bridge_saved or
# ch1_bridge_fell. Later caravans, prices and the ending reference it.
~ bridge_saved
Bran: Stood on it myself, rain and all, river right up under the boards. Didn't creak once. That's going in the ledger, lad, in my best hand.

~ bridge_fell
Bran: Heard it go about an hour ago. Sounded like the whole hill sighing.
[if ch1_bridge_evacuated] Bran: Nobody was on it. I wrote that down first, before the rest, because that part's yours.
[if not ch1_bridge_evacuated] Bran: Tobb's cart was halfway over when it went. He got out. The cart didn't, and his leg's not right. I've written the hour by his name.

# The staged boar fight (no side-scroll arena for it yet).
~ boar_fight_staged
do boar_charge
System: CORRUPTED BOAR — CHARGING.
Elara: It can't turn once it's running! Jump it!
do boar_stunned
Elara: Now, while it's dizzy! Jump, then {move_down} and {attack} on its back!
do boar_pogo
do boar_charge
Elara: Again! I'll wall it in!
do boar_pogo
System: ELITE DEFEATED.
Kaelen: ...It was still trying to get back to the nest. Every charge, it kept turning toward—
Elara: I know. I saw.

# Y1-P0-T13c: back in the village after the boar fight in the arena. Its two
# closing lines, moved here word for word from boar_fight_staged (unplayed now).
~ boar_fight_after
Kaelen: ...It was still trying to get back to the nest. Every charge, it kept turning toward—
Elara: I know. I saw.

# Kaelen stayed in the village. Time passes; the field gets closed without him.
~ field_refused_aftermath
do time_passes
Mara: They got it closed. Bran's lads, the Pell boys, and half a fence. Took them till the bread burned.
Mara: Jory's arm's broken. He'll live. He's already telling it bigger than it was.
set ch1_north_field_injuries
